// DOS executable: the MZ header, 28 bytes, and then two numbers
// that decide everything. e_cblp counts 16-byte paragraphs of
// relocation table and e_cp counts 512-byte pages of load module,
// and the header plus those two has to account for the whole file.
//
// The entry point is a segment and an offset, e_cs and e_ip, and
// the code here starts at offset 0 of the load module -- which is
// why e_ip is 0 rather than 0x100. Nothing prints; the code is in
// the segment.
//
// Hello World! is the load module's own bytes.
//
// dos_exe: 548 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

